                        "tags": [
                            "comparative"
                        ],
                        "form": "more womanish"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "e0a8aa7b-466e-4161-9c72-7e98ea6f5d84",
                        "entry_id": "a9083e09-6d44-384e-b772-9b8449c3e954",
                        "tags": [
                            "superlative"
                        ],
                        "form": "most womanish"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "7aaebf18-6ebd-3e4f-b54a-179e3b71aa5b",
                        "entry_id": "a9083e09-6d44-384e-b772-9b8449c3e954",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Characteristic of a woman; effeminate, feminine."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "derogatory",
                            "often"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "9a06ee09-2ed7-4336-907f-2cf698fe0316",
                                "sense_id": "7aaebf18-6ebd-3e4f-b54a-179e3b71aa5b",
                                "text": "[…] Romans novv / Haue Thevves, and Limbes, like to their Anceſtors; / But vvoe the vvhile, our Fathers mindes are dead, / And vve are gouern'd vvith our Mothers ſpirits, / Our yoake, and ſufferance, ſhevv vs VVomaniſh."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "15fd7a84-3f0a-4ae3-816f-c0add0f8a70f",
                                "sense_id": "7aaebf18-6ebd-3e4f-b54a-179e3b71aa5b",
                                "text": "The Fence was a proper Park paling in excellent condition; with clusters of fine Elms, or rows of old Thorns following its line almost every where.—Almost must be stipulated—for there were vacant spaces & through one of these, Charlotte as soon as they entered the Enclosure, caught a glimpse over the pales of something White & Womanish in the field on the other side;—it was a something which immediately brought Miss B. into her head—& stepping to the pales, she saw indeed—& very decidedly, in spite of the Mist; Miss B—seated, not far before her, at the foot of the bank which sloped down from the outside of the Paling & which a narrow Path seemed to skirt along;—Miss Brereton seated, apparently very composedly—& Sir E. D. by her side.",
                                "translation": "Sanditon",
                                "english": "Sanditon"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "1f8fa833-e0a2-47b9-8968-1bb9dea6da8f",
                                "sense_id": "7aaebf18-6ebd-3e4f-b54a-179e3b71aa5b",
                                "text": "I don't very much wonder at her fright. We have met before; but I owe her no grudge, and we must not wait for womanish fear."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "0816142c-97c5-48c7-bf4f-80d2d57b83c3",
                                "sense_id": "7aaebf18-6ebd-3e4f-b54a-179e3b71aa5b",
                                "text": "Friends are a comfort in misfortune, but one should not make them unhappy by seeking their sympathy, as is done by women and womanish men."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "41c8f73a-a348-464c-acf4-b369fe2f7177",
                                "sense_id": "7aaebf18-6ebd-3e4f-b54a-179e3b71aa5b",
                                "text": "Perhaps he did too, for he turned scarlet and turned his face away to the wall, with a womanish gesture of shyness."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "af9602a6-992c-3acb-920a-55bd6fb2d197",
                        "entry_id": "a9083e09-6d44-384e-b772-9b8449c3e954",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Carried out by or pertaining to a woman."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "bbb1d2ec-881e-4f03-9ece-393968dd17ff",
                                "sense_id": "af9602a6-992c-3acb-920a-55bd6fb2d197",
                                "text": "And gan recomfort her in her rude vvyſe, / VVith vvomaniſh compaſſion of her plaint, / VViping the teares from her ſuffuſed eyes, […]"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
